From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIVI appliance
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: copy frames when downstream is system memory

The v4l2codecs decoders always allocate their output from an internal
DMABuf pool; only a downstream that needs neither a plain layout nor a
system-memory handoff gets a copy. A converter (or any element that
negotiates plain video/x-raw without the DMABuf feature) therefore reads
every pixel straight out of an uncached dmabuf mapping. On the Allwinner
H616 that makes videoconvert's NV12 -> BGRx step take ~170 ms per
800x480 frame (~6 fps, measured on hardware), which stalls the whole
video path even though the decode itself is hardware and fast.

Set sysmem_output from the negotiated caps and have the existing
copy_frames path land the frame in the base class's system-memory pool:
one memcpy per frame (~5 ms) and every later conversion reads cached
memory. A DMABuf consumer (a GPU-backed sink) keeps zero-copy.

The same change is applied to the H.264 and H.265 decoders, the two the
appliance's Android Auto/CarPlay path uses.
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
@@ -86,6 +86,8 @@
   GstV4l2CodecPool *src_pool;
   gint min_pool_size;
   gboolean has_videometa;
+  /* Downstream negotiated plain system memory, not DMABuf caps. */
+  gboolean sysmem_output;
   gboolean streaming;
   gboolean interlaced;
   gboolean need_sequence;
@@ -455,6 +457,14 @@
     return FALSE;
   }
 
+  /* The internal pool only hands out DMABufs. A downstream that negotiated
+   * plain system memory cannot consume them cheaply: on SoCs with
+   * non-coherent DMA the dmabuf mapping is uncached, so a converter's
+   * per-pixel reads stall (measured ~170 ms per 800x480 frame on the
+   * Allwinner H616). Read the frame back into the base class's
+   * system-memory pool instead, one memcpy per frame. */
+  self->sysmem_output = !gst_video_is_dma_drm_caps (caps);
+
   if (gst_query_get_n_allocation_pools (query) > 0)
     gst_query_parse_nth_allocation_pool (query, 0, NULL, NULL, &min, NULL);
 
@@ -944,7 +954,10 @@
   }
 
   /* Check if we can zero-copy buffers */
-  if (!self->has_videometa) {
+  if (self->sysmem_output) {
+    GST_INFO_OBJECT (self, "System memory downstream, copying frames");
+    self->copy_frames = TRUE;
+  } else if (!self->has_videometa) {
     GstVideoInfo ref_vinfo;
     gint i;
 
